<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.9.1: Solving Equations Using Opposite Operations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01885</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.9.1: Solving Equations Using Opposite Operations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>97168160-51ba-4208-96bf-6134c1a490ef</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Solve each equation mentally. Then, enter your answer to check it.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="859dc981-9328-4243-9d12-9fe5fdf40386" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>\(40-8=40+n\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(– 8\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(– 8\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="ebd32831-f7ba-4c60-b2a7-d3e10b068b33" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>\(25+-100=25-n\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(100\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(100\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="b0f099ec-cdea-44ac-a2da-68bb983f3215" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>\(-3- \frac {1}{2}=3+ \frac {1}{2}n\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(– 13\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(– 13\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="ef778c92-62b0-4cae-9b82-28fc485f40db" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>\(72-n=72+6\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(– 6\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(– 6\).</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
